The plate is a square-ish plate, roughly 20 cm across (about 340 px in the image). It holds 6 pieces of cooked potato or turnip, each about 3-4 cm long and 2-3 cm thick. Each piece is roughly 15-20 g, so the total is about 100 g. The pieces look glazed or lightly browned, as if braised or pan-fried, and there is no visible sauce.

I judged this to be braised daikon radish or potato. Potato would be about 90 kcal per 100 g and radish less, so I used 80 kcal per 100 g.

